# feat(email): add Get-IRTEmailSearch manager

## Summary

This branch finishes the email-search workflow. `New-IRTEmailSearch`
already creates and starts a search; the new `Get-IRTEmailSearch` lets an
analyst come back to existing searches and actually work them — run, wait,
review hits, purge, and clean up — without dropping to the raw
`*-ComplianceSearch*` cmdlets. It also hardens the create side and unifies
terminology on "email search."

## What changed

**New: `Get-IRTEmailSearch` (interactive manager)**
- Lists existing searches in an aligned, numbered table (name + status),
  and shows each search's item count once it has been viewed this session.
- Per-search action menu: **Start**, **Wait for completion**,
  **Results**, **Purge email**, **Wait for purge**, **Delete search**.
- **Results** reads the search's structured `SearchStatistics` JSON
  (per-mailbox name / item count / size). This needs only ordinary
  Compliance Search permissions — *not* the eDiscovery Preview role — so it
  works for analysts who can run searches but can't preview. It always
  exports an autosized Excel workbook (opened on save) titled with the
  search name, tenant domain, and run time.
- **Purge** asks SoftDelete vs HardDelete first, then confirms, and
  suppresses the native Exchange confirmation prompt. **Wait for purge**
  monitors the purge action to completion.
- Main-menu **bulk delete** removes every search whose name starts with the
  configured prefix, after listing them and confirming.
- Detailed search objects are cached per session: a completed (immutable)
  search is reused instead of re-fetched, and the wait loops check status
  before sleeping so an already-finished search/purge returns immediately.

**New: `Get-EmailSearchResult` (private helper)**
- Parses `SearchStatistics` into one row per mailbox with hits. Carries a
  `# FIXME` for a future opt-in Graph mode that would re-query per mailbox
  for message-level detail and folder (trash) info via `Mail.Read`.

**Hardened `New-IRTEmailSearch`**
- Strips characters Exchange rejects from the generated name (notably the
  `*` / `?` wildcards) so a valid query like `From:microsoft*` no longer
  crashes creation. The wildcard still works in the query itself.
- Wraps create/start so a failed `New-ComplianceSearch` stops with a clear
  error instead of falling through to `Start-ComplianceSearch` on a null
  object and falsely reporting success.
- On a name collision it now offers a new name (Enter accepts the next free
  `Name N`, or type your own); `-Force` picks the next free name instead of
  overwriting. Nothing is ever overwritten.

**Other**
- New `EmailSearchNamePrefix` config setting (default `IRT: `).
- The interactive builder now explains KQL From-field tokenization and
  trailing-wildcard behavior when entering a From value.
- Standardized user-facing wording on "email search" (kept literal cmdlet
  names and the Exchange "Compliance Search" role name).
- `tests/Test-ExplicitModuleImport.ps1`: mapped the offline-undiscoverable
  `Get-/New-ComplianceSearchAction` cmdlets to `ExchangeOnlineManagement`.
- Added `Scripts/Debug/Get-IRTEmailSearch_DEBUG.ps1` for live-tenant runs.

## Testing

- Offline Pester suite: 246 passed, 0 failed (2 skipped, online not run).
- Formatting/lint on changed files: LineLength, BacktickContinuation, and
  PSScriptAnalyzer all clean.
- `Get-EmailSearchResult`'s `SearchStatistics` parsing was verified against
  a real exported search result (6 mailboxes, 121 items).

## Notes

- Built artifacts (`M365IncidentResponseTools.psd1/.psm1`, root `Data/`,
  the `.xlsx` templates) were intentionally not committed; regenerate with
  `.\Build.ps1`.
- Folder/trash detection is deliberately out of scope here — it requires
  either the eDiscovery Preview role or the future Graph mode noted by the
  `# FIXME`s. The current Results view is aggregate-only by design.
